== The Solberg family of Minneapolis

#block(breakable: false, below: 1.36em)[
Most of what is known about the Solberg family comes from two recordings made in March 2023, when Tamsin Penhallow asked her grandmother #refp("ruth-kessler") about both sides of her family.#src("ruth-interview-2023")
]

#block(breakable: false, below: 1.36em)[
Ruth remembered that her husband's father, Olaf Solberg, was born in Minneapolis about 1899 to parents from Norway.#src("olaf-birth") He drove a streetcar there for many years.#src("olaf-streetcar") Olaf married Hilda Marie Berg in 1928.#src("solberg-berg-marriage-1928") Hilda was also born in Minneapolis.#src("hilda-birth") Their son Arne was born on 3 February 1932, and their daughter Ingrid in 1935.#src("arne-birth-1932")#src("ingrid-solberg::ingrid-birth")
]

#block(breakable: false, below: 1.36em)[
The names of Olaf's parents are not known, nor where in Norway they came from.#src("olaf-birth") Ruth said that Olaf died in 1968 and Hilda in 1990, both in Minneapolis.#src("olaf-death")#src("hilda-death")
]

== The Kessler family of Madison

#block(breakable: false, below: 1.36em)[
Ruth's parents were Herman Friedrich Kessler and Anna Vogel. Ruth said her father was born on the east side of Madison.#src("herman-birth-ruth") The couple married in Madison in 1929.#src("kessler-vogel-marriage-1929")
]

#block(breakable: false, below: 1.36em)[
The 1940 census found the family in Madison.#src("herman-census-1940") Herman, aged thirty-four, was a cooper making barrels for a brewery.#src("herman-cooper-1940") At home were Anna, thirty-two, their son Walter, nine, and Ruth, six.#src("anna-census-1940")#src("walter-kessler::walter-census-1940")#src("ruth-census-1940") The census gives Wisconsin as the birthplace of both Herman and Anna.#src("anna-census-1940") The names of Herman's parents are not known.
]

#block(breakable: false, below: 1.36em)[
Anna's apple kuchen passed from mother to daughter. Ruth later gave the recipe to Joan Penhallow, who typed it into her 1995 booklet.#src("anna-kuchen-1995") Herman died in 1979, and Anna in 1998, aged ninety-one.#src("herman-death")#src("anna-death") Ruth's brother Walter died in 2010.#src("walter-kessler::walter-death")
]

== Arne and Ruth

#block(breakable: false, below: 1.36em)[
Arne came to Madison to study engineering and stayed to work for the state highway department.#src("arne-engineer") He and Ruth married in Madison on 22 June 1957.#src("solberg-kessler-marriage-1957") Their daughter #refp("karin-solberg") was born in 1961, and their son Paul in 1963.#src("karin-solberg::karin-birth")#src("paul-solberg::paul-birth")
]

#block(breakable: false, below: 1.36em)[
Arne died in Madison in 2015.#src("arne-death-2015") The recordings Ruth made with Tamsin eight years later are the main source for this chapter, and almost every date in it rests on her memory.#src("ruth-interview-2023")
]
